course: dictionary
lesson: 14414
title: Overhang: sticking out
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An overhang is a part that sticks out over something below it. «The roof overhangs the front door, so we stay dry in the rain.» The roof reaches out past the wall, and the part that sticks out is the overhang.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Rain and dry tell you the roof keeps water off. «The cliff overhangs the beach, so keep away from the bottom.» The rock sticks out over the sand, and the warning tells you it could fall.
explain: Overhang is a verb as well as a noun, and its past form is overhung. «The branches overhung the path.» To check your meaning, swap in "stuck out over": if the sentence still makes sense, you have it.
fact: To overhang means to stick out over something below.
fact: An overhang is the part that sticks out, like a roof edge or a rock ledge.
fact: Overhang can be a verb or a noun: «The ledge overhangs the river.» and «The overhang kept the rain off.»
fact: The verb forms are overhang, overhangs, overhung and overhanging.
fact: A cliff overhang may fall, so it is unsafe to stand under or on it.
exercise: «The roof overhangs the front door, so we stay dry in the rain.» What does overhangs mean here? | Falls into the garden | *Sticks out over something below | Is painted bright red | Hides the door completely
exercise: «The climber pulled herself up under the overhang.» Find the noun in this sentence. | pulled | herself | *overhang | climber
exercise: «Stay away from the cliff, because the overhang might fall.» Why is it unsafe? | It is too small to see | *It could fall on you | It is covered in soft grass
test: «The branches overhung the path, so we had to duck.» What does overhung mean? | *Stuck out over the path | Was cut down | Was lying flat on the ground | Was covered in snow
test: «The rain ran off the roof overhang and not down the wall.» What job does the overhang do? | Holds up the chimney | Lets sunlight into the walls | Makes the house heavier | *Keeps rain off the walls
exam: «The walkers sheltered under the rock overhang from the storm.» What is an overhang in this sentence? | A loud noise in the storm | A river crossing | *A rock that sticks out over the ground, giving shelter | A hole dug in the ground
